LIB_LOAD("qv",{"qv1":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who wrote Quo Vadis?","o":["Henryk Sienkiewicz","John Bunyan","Charles Sheldon","C. S. Lewis"],"why":"A Polish writer who won the Nobel Prize."},{"q":"About how long after Jesus rose is the story set?","o":["About thirty years","About three hundred years","About three years","About a thousand years"],"why":"Around A.D. 64."},{"q":"What is Petronius's nickname?","o":["The Arbiter of Elegance","The Great Builder","The Lion","The Wise"],"why":"Rome copied his style."},{"q":"Where were the Lygians from?","o":["The far north, in today's Poland","Egypt","Nigeria","Greece"],"why":"Lygia's father was their king."},{"q":"What did Lygia draw in the sand?","o":["A fish","A cross","A sword","A crown"],"why":"The Christians' secret sign."},{"q":"Who was Acte?","o":["A kind freedwoman who befriended Lygia","Nero's mother","Lygia's sister","A gladiator"],"why":"A friend in the palace."},{"q":"What was Nero proud of?","o":["His singing and poetry","His kindness","His honesty","His humility"],"why":"Everyone had to clap."},{"q":"How did Ursus stop Vinicius at the feast?","o":["He silently carried Lygia away","He shouted","He fought the guards","He called the police"],"why":"Strong and gentle."},{"q":"What happened to the litter in the dark street?","o":["Christians rescued Lygia from it","It fell into the river","Nero took it","It arrived safely"],"why":"When the torches were relit, it was empty."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"What time I am afraid, I will ___ in thee.\"","o":["trust","hide","run","sleep"],"why":"Psalm 56:3."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'ICHTHYS', the Greek word for fish, stand for?","o":["Jesus Christ, God's Son, Saviour","Rome Is Great","Long Live Caesar","Peace Be With You"],"why":"That's why the fish was the Christians' sign."},"choices":[{"title":"A 'no' is a no","q":"At a party, you see a boy keep pulling a girl to dance even though she has said no twice. His friends are laughing.","o":[{"t":"Step in calmly, help her move away, and tell an adult if he won't stop.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Ursus, you protected someone who was being treated as a prize."},{"t":"Laugh along. It's just a joke.","f":"It's not a joke to her. A 'no' is a no."},{"t":"Look away. It's not your business.","f":"Sometimes it becomes your business when someone needs help."}]},{"title":"Treated like a trophy","q":"Someone in your class says, \"I'll get her to be my girlfriend. She'll make me look good.\"","o":[{"t":"Say, \"She's a person, not a trophy,\" and change the conversation.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Vinicius saw Lygia as a prize. You saw a person."},{"t":"Help him plan it.","f":"That's using someone to make yourself look good."},{"t":"Say nothing, but warn her secretly.","f":"Warning her is kind, but speaking the truth to him matters too."}]},{"title":"The only believer","q":"You join a new school club. Everyone mocks religion, and someone asks, \"You don't actually believe all that, do you?\"","o":[{"t":"Answer kindly and honestly: \"Yes, I do. Jesus means a lot to me.\"","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Lygia and Pomponia, quiet faith can be brave faith."},{"t":"Say, \"No, of course not,\" to fit in.","f":"Peter once did that too, and wept afterwards."},{"t":"Mock religion with them.","f":"That's denying the One who loves you."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"rome","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of Quo Vadis in real life."},{"sc":"fishsand","n":"🐟 Your faith matters, even if you're the only believer in the room."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"🙏 When you're afraid, say Psalm 56:3: \"What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.\""},{"sc":"banquet","n":"🤍 People are never prizes. Respect every 'no', and guard your own purity."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"🤝 Be like the Christians who rescued Lygia: when someone is in danger, pray and act."}],"stops":{"qv1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"rome","n":"Rome, about thirty years after Jesus rose from the dead. The greatest city in the world, ruled by an emperor called {Nero}."},{"sc":"rome","n":"Henryk Sienkiewicz, a Polish writer who later won the Nobel Prize, set this famous story there. Some characters were real people. Others he imagined."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Marcus Vinicius is a young {tribune}, just home from the wars. He is brave, rich and handsome, and used to getting whatever he wants."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"His uncle is Petronius, the most stylish man in Rome. People call him the '{Arbiter of Elegance}'. Even Nero copies him."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"vinicius","e":"big","t":"Uncle, I've seen a girl. Her name is Lygia. I can't stop thinking about her. I must have her."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Lygia is the daughter of a king of the {Lygians}, a people far to the north. As a little girl she was sent to Rome as a {hostage}."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"She grew up in the home of a general named Aulus Plautius and his wife, {Pomponia Graecina}, who loved her like a daughter."},{"sc":"fishsand","n":"When Vinicius met Lygia in the garden, he talked boldly about love. Lygia said little. With a reed, she quietly drew a fish in the sand."},{"sc":"fishsand","n":"Vinicius had no idea what it meant. But for Lygia, {the fish} was a secret sign. It meant: I follow Jesus Christ. One day that little fish would lead Vinicius somewhere he never expected."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"pomponia","e":"worried","t":"Lygia, be careful. Not everyone who draws a fish knows what it means."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Pomponia and Lygia were secret Christians. In Nero's Rome, that was a dangerous thing to be."}],"quote":{"text":"Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.","who":"Matthew 16:16","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Faith in a hard place","text":"Lygia and Pomponia followed Jesus quietly in a city that worshipped the emperor and pleasure. The fish was their sign: Jesus Christ, God's Son, Saviour. You may be the only believer in a room. Your faith still matters there."},"think":"Why do you think early Christians used a secret sign like the fish? Are there places today where following Jesus is dangerous?","quiz":[{"q":"Who was emperor of Rome in this story?","o":["Nero","Julius Caesar","Augustus","Pharaoh"],"why":"A cruel, vain emperor."},{"q":"Who is Marcus Vinicius?","o":["A young Roman tribune, used to getting what he wants","A Christian bishop","A slave","Lygia's brother"],"why":"Brave, rich and proud."},{"q":"Why was Lygia living in Rome?","o":["She had been sent as a hostage","She was born there","She was a slave","She came to study"],"why":"She was the daughter of a Lygian king."},{"q":"What did the fish mean to Christians?","o":["Jesus Christ, God's Son, Saviour","Let's go fishing","Dinner time","Danger"],"why":"ICHTHYS spells it in Greek."},{"q":"Who raised Lygia like a daughter?","o":["Pomponia Graecina and Aulus Plautius","Nero","Petronius","Ursus"],"why":"Pomponia was a secret Christian."}]},"qv1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Petronius came up with a clever, cruel plan to get Lygia for his nephew."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"petronius","e":"smirk","t":"Leave it to me. I'll tell Caesar she's a hostage who belongs in the palace. Then he can give her to you."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Soon soldiers arrived at Pomponia's house with an order from {Caesar}: Lygia must go to the emperor's palace."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"pomponia","e":"worried","t":"My child. I cannot stop them. But remember: Christ is with you, even in Caesar's house."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Nero's palace was full of gold, marble, music and danger. Everyone there was watching everyone else."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Lygia was alone and afraid. But she found a friend: Acte, a kind freedwoman who had once been close to Nero. Acte was not a Christian, but she had heard about Jesus and was gentle."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"acte","e":"worried","t":"Be careful here, Lygia. In this palace, a smile can be a trap."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"lygia","e":"worried","t":"I'm afraid. But I will pray. God can see me here too."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"With Lygia came her faithful servant, Ursus, a giant from her own people. He was as strong as a bear, as gentle as a lamb, and a Christian too. He had sworn to protect her."}],"quote":{"text":"What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.","who":"Psalm 56:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Afraid, but trusting","text":"Lygia was taken from her home into the most dangerous place in Rome. She was afraid, and she didn't pretend not to be. But she chose to trust God. Courage isn't the absence of fear. It's trusting God while you're afraid."},"think":"Lygia found one friend in the palace, Acte. Why is one kind friend so important in a frightening new place?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Petronius's plan?","o":["Get Caesar to bring Lygia to the palace, then give her to Vinicius","Help Lygia escape","Send Lygia home","Become a Christian"],"why":"Clever and cruel."},{"q":"What did Pomponia tell Lygia?","o":["Christ is with you, even in Caesar's house","Run away now","Forget your faith","Marry Vinicius"],"why":"God goes with us."},{"q":"Who became Lygia's friend in the palace?","o":["Acte","Nero","Petronius","Poppaea"],"why":"A kind freedwoman."},{"q":"Who is Ursus?","o":["Lygia's giant, gentle protector","A Roman soldier","Nero's cook","A lion"],"why":"Strong as a bear, gentle as a lamb."},{"q":"What does Psalm 56:3 say?","o":["What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee","Never be afraid","Run when you are afraid","Fear everyone"],"why":"Trust God while afraid."}]},"qv1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"That night, Nero held a huge feast. Roses fell from the ceiling. Wine flowed. Guests ate until they were sick, then ate again."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"nero","e":"big","t":"Silence! Your emperor will now sing for you!"},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Nero sang badly. Everybody clapped wildly. In Nero's Rome, telling the truth about his singing could cost you your life."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Lygia sat at the table in horror. The guests were drunk, rude and shameless. This was nothing like the quiet, prayerful home she knew."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Vinicius sat beside her. He had been drinking. He leaned close and grabbed her, trying to kiss her, as if she already belonged to him."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"lygia","e":"shock","t":"Please, stop! Let me go!"},{"sc":"banquet","w":"vinicius","e":"smirk","t":"Soon you'll be mine anyway. Caesar has promised you to me."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Then a huge shadow fell over the table. Ursus had stepped forward. He said nothing. He just lifted Lygia gently away and carried her out of the hall."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"Vinicius saw Lygia as a prize to be won. A beautiful thing to own. He didn't see her as a person with her own heart, her own faith and her own choices."},{"sc":"praetorium","n":"That is how many people still treat others. But God made every person in his image. Nobody is a prize for someone else to grab."}],"quote":{"text":"Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on the Lord out of a pure heart.","who":"2 Timothy 2:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"People are not prizes","text":"At Nero's feast, Vinicius treated Lygia like an object he was owed. That's never love. Real love respects the other person's 'no', their body and their faith. Guard your own purity, and never treat anyone as a prize."},"think":"What's the difference between love and wanting to own someone? How can we tell which one we're seeing in films, songs or real life?","proverb":{"text":"Ìwà lẹwà.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Character is beauty. What makes a person truly beautiful is who they are inside."},"quiz":[{"q":"Why did everyone clap for Nero's bad singing?","o":["Telling the truth could cost them their lives","He sang beautifully","They were deaf","He paid them"],"why":"Fear made the whole court dishonest."},{"q":"How did Lygia feel at the feast?","o":["Horrified","Excited","Bored","Sleepy"],"why":"It was nothing like her prayerful home."},{"q":"What did Vinicius do?","o":["Grabbed her as if she belonged to him","Prayed with her","Defended her","Left early"],"why":"He saw her as a prize."},{"q":"Who carried Lygia out of the hall?","o":["Ursus","Nero","Petronius","Acte"],"why":"Silently and gently."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb 'Ìwà lẹwà' mean?","o":["Character is beauty","Money is power","Food is life","Strength is beauty"],"why":"Lygia's beauty was more than her face."}]},"qv1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"praetorium","n":"The next evening, Lygia was to be carried in a {litter} to the house of Vinicius. He was planning a feast to welcome her."},{"sc":"praetorium","w":"lygia","e":"worried","t":"Acte, I would rather die than go to him like this. Please, God, help me."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The litter set off through the dark streets of Rome, with slaves carrying it and Ursus walking beside it."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Suddenly, in a narrow street, a crowd of men rushed out of the shadows. The slaves dropped their torches. There was shouting and confusion."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"When the torches were lit again, the litter was empty. Lygia was gone. And so was Ursus."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The men who rescued her were Christians. They had heard of her danger, prayed, and come to help one of their own."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"vinicius","e":"frown","t":"Gone? She was stolen from me? I'll search every house in Rome until I find her!"},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Vinicius was furious. His pride was hurt, and his 'prize' had escaped. He swore he would find her, whatever it took."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"He didn't know it yet, but his search would lead him to something far bigger than Lygia. It would lead him to Christ."}],"quote":{"text":"The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.","who":"Psalm 34:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God's family shows up","text":"Lygia prayed, and God answered through his people: brave Christians who came out at night to rescue her. The church is a family. When one member is in danger, the others pray and act."},"think":"The Christians risked their lives for a girl they barely knew. What does that teach us about being a church family?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Lygia being taken in the litter?","o":["To Vinicius's house","Back to Pomponia","To the arena","To the sea"],"why":"Against her will."},{"q":"What did Lygia say she would rather do than go to him like that?","o":["Die","Dance","Eat","Sing"],"why":"She would not be treated as a prize."},{"q":"Who rescued Lygia?","o":["A group of Christians","Roman soldiers","Nero","Petronius"],"why":"God's family showed up."},{"q":"How did Vinicius react?","o":["He was furious and swore to find her","He was relieved","He became a Christian at once","He forgot about her"],"why":"His pride was hurt."},{"q":"What does Psalm 34:7 say the angel of the Lord does?","o":["Camps around those who fear him and delivers them","Sleeps","Leaves them","Punishes them"],"why":"God guards his own."}]}}},"qv2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was Chilo willing to do for gold?","o":["Lie and betray anyone","Nothing","Pray","Work hard honestly"],"why":"A sly 'philosopher'."},{"q":"How did Chilo know Lygia was a Christian?","o":["She had drawn a fish","She told him","She wore a cross","Nero told him"],"why":"The secret sign."},{"q":"What had Chilo done to Glaucus long ago?","o":["Betrayed him and his family","Saved his life","Taught him","Built his house"],"why":"Glaucus was left for dead."},{"q":"Where was the secret night meeting?","o":["The Ostrianum","The arena","Nero's palace","The river"],"why":"Outside the city, by torchlight."},{"q":"How many times had Peter denied Jesus?","o":["Three","One","Seven","None"],"why":"And Jesus forgave him."},{"q":"Who was Croton?","o":["A famous gladiator","A Christian","A doctor","A senator"],"why":"Ursus defeated him."},{"q":"Why did Ursus stop before striking Vinicius?","o":["Lygia cried, 'Christ forbids it!'","He got tired","Soldiers came","He slipped"],"why":"Strength under control."},{"q":"What injury did Vinicius suffer?","o":["A broken arm","A broken leg","None","A lost eye"],"why":"Glaucus set it."},{"q":"Which apostle visited Vinicius besides Peter?","o":["Paul","John","Judas","Matthew"],"why":"Paul of Tarsus."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with ___.\"","o":["good","anger","power","silence"],"why":"Romans 12:21."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Who warned Lygia to guard her heart?","o":["Crispus","Chilo","Nero","Acte"],"why":"A strict but caring elder."},"choices":[{"title":"Easy money","q":"Someone offers you ₦5,000 to tell them which classmate posted an anonymous complaint about a teacher. You know who it was.","o":[{"t":"Refuse the money and keep it to yourself.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Gaskiya ta fi kwabo. Don't be a Chilo."},{"t":"Take it. It's only information.","f":"That's exactly how Chilo started: selling people for gold."},{"t":"Make up a name and take the money.","f":"Now you've lied and cheated."}]},{"title":"Repaying evil with good","q":"A girl who has bullied you all term falls and hurts her ankle on the sports field. Nobody is helping her.","o":[{"t":"Help her up and take her to the nurse.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Glaucus bandaging Vinicius, you overcame evil with good."},{"t":"Walk past. She deserves it.","f":"The Christians had every reason to say that about Vinicius."},{"t":"Laugh, like she would have.","f":"That's being overcome by evil."}]},{"title":"Anger in your fists","q":"Someone shoves your little brother at the bus stop. You're much bigger than him, and you feel your fists clench.","o":[{"t":"Stand between them, protect your brother, and say firmly, \"Stop.\" Then tell an adult.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Ursus, protect without destroying. Strength under control."},{"t":"Beat him up so he learns.","f":"Ursus could have, and chose not to."},{"t":"Do nothing.","f":"Protecting the weak matters too."}]},{"title":"Faith before feelings","q":"You really like someone who is kind and funny, but they mock your faith and want you to stop going to church.","o":[{"t":"Be kind, but don't let a crush pull you away from God. Talk to a trusted adult.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Lygia put Christ first, even when her heart hurt."},{"t":"Stop going to church to keep them happy.","f":"Lygia chose differently, and it was the right choice."},{"t":"Pretend you don't believe when you're with them.","f":"That's living two lives."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"rome","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of Quo Vadis in real life."},{"sc":"rome","n":"💰 Never sell the truth or a friend for money. Truth is worth more."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"🔥 Our faith rests on eyewitnesses: Jesus really lived, died and rose."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"🐻 Strength under control: protect others, but don't let anger rule your hands."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🩹 Love your enemies. Kindness can do what arguments can't."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"💛 Put Christ before your feelings, even when your heart is pulling you."}],"stops":{"qv2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"rome","n":"Vinicius offered a big reward to anyone who could find Lygia. And one man came hurrying to collect it."},{"sc":"rome","w":"chilo","e":"smirk","t":"Noble tribune! I am {Chilo} Chilonides, a philosopher. For a little gold, I can find anyone in Rome."},{"sc":"rome","n":"Chilo was a sly Greek with a dirty cloak and crumbs in his beard. He told lies as easily as he breathed, and he would sell anyone for money."},{"sc":"fishsand","w":"vinicius","e":"worried","t":"Before she disappeared, she drew a fish in the sand. Does that mean anything?"},{"sc":"fishsand","w":"chilo","e":"big","t":"A fish? Ha! That's the secret sign of the Christians! Your Lygia is one of them. Leave it to me."},{"sc":"rome","n":"So Chilo pretended to be a Christian. He drew fish signs, asked questions, and slowly worked his way into their circles."},{"sc":"rome","n":"There was one Christian Chilo was terrified of meeting: a doctor named {Glaucus}. Years before, Chilo had betrayed him. Glaucus had been left for dead, and his wife and children were sold as slaves."},{"sc":"rome","w":"chilo","e":"worried","t":"If Glaucus recognises me, I'm finished. But the gold, the gold..."},{"sc":"rome","n":"Then Chilo heard something big. The Christians were going to meet secretly at night, outside the city, to hear a great {apostle} speak: a man who had walked with Jesus himself."}],"quote":{"text":"Lying lips are abomination to the LORD: but they that deal truly are his delight.","who":"Proverbs 12:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Don't sell the truth","text":"Chilo would say anything and betray anyone for gold. Lies may pay quickly, but they make a person small and afraid, always looking over their shoulder. Truth is worth more than any reward."},"think":"Chilo was always afraid of being found out. How do lies make a person's life more frightening, not less?","proverb":{"text":"Gaskiya ta fi kwabo.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Truth is worth more than money."},"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Chilo come to Vinicius?","o":["To collect the reward for finding Lygia","To become a Christian","To warn Lygia","To sell bread"],"why":"He would do anything for gold."},{"q":"What did Chilo say the fish meant?","o":["The secret sign of the Christians","A fisherman's mark","A curse","A love letter"],"why":"He knew the sign."},{"q":"How did Chilo get close to the Christians?","o":["He pretended to be one","He asked the emperor","He joined the army","He paid them"],"why":"A liar in disguise."},{"q":"Who was Chilo afraid of meeting?","o":["Glaucus, the doctor he had betrayed","Nero","Ursus","Lygia"],"why":"His past was catching up with him."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb say?","o":["Truth is worth more than money","Money talks","Gold is king","Lies are clever"],"why":"Gaskiya ta fi kwabo."}]},"qv2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"That night, Vinicius wrapped himself in a dark cloak with a hood. With Chilo and a huge {gladiator} named {Croton}, he crept out to the {Ostrianum}."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"By torchlight, thousands of people had gathered: slaves and free people, rich and poor, old and young. They sang quietly together."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Then an old man stood up on a stone. His hair and beard were white, and he spoke like a fisherman. It was Peter, the apostle."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"I saw him. I walked with him. I saw him heal the sick. I saw him die on the cross. And on the third day, I saw him alive."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"peter","e":"worried","t":"When he was arrested, I denied him three times. But he forgave me, and he asked me, 'Do you love me?'"},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"He told us to love one another. Not only our friends, but our enemies too. To pray for those who hurt us."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Vinicius couldn't believe his ears. Love your enemies? In Rome, you crushed your enemies. That was strength."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"vinicius","e":"shock","t":"What kind of god asks people to forgive those who hurt them? This is madness, or something greater than I've ever heard."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Then, in the torchlight, he saw a face he knew. Lygia was there in the crowd, listening, her eyes shining."}],"quote":{"text":"For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty.","who":"2 Peter 1:16","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Eyewitness faith","text":"Peter wasn't sharing a nice idea. He was telling what he had seen with his own eyes. Christian faith rests on real events: Jesus lived, died and rose again. And his teaching turned the world upside down: love even your enemies."},"think":"Why do you think 'love your enemies' sounded like madness to a Roman soldier? Does it still sound strange today?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did Vinicius take to the Ostrianum?","o":["Chilo and Croton","Petronius and Nero","Ursus and Lygia","Nobody"],"why":"A spy and a gladiator."},{"q":"Who was gathered there?","o":["Thousands of all kinds: slaves, free, rich and poor","Only soldiers","Only priests","Only children"],"why":"The church was for everyone."},{"q":"Who spoke to them?","o":["The apostle Peter","Nero","Petronius","Chilo"],"why":"A fisherman who walked with Jesus."},{"q":"What did Peter say he had seen?","o":["Jesus heal, die and rise again","A dream","A statue","Nothing"],"why":"He was an eyewitness."},{"q":"Which teaching shocked Vinicius most?","o":["Love your enemies","Eat well","Obey Caesar","Get rich"],"why":"In Rome you crushed your enemies."}]},"qv2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"After the meeting, Vinicius followed Lygia through the dark streets to a small house across the river. Chilo slipped away, afraid of trouble."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"vinicius","e":"frown","t":"Croton, when I give the word, grab the girl. If the giant tries to stop you, deal with him."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"croton","e":"smirk","t":"No one in Rome can beat Croton."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"They burst into the house. But in the doorway stood Ursus."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Croton was the strongest gladiator in Rome. But Ursus wrapped his great arms around him and squeezed, and the gladiator never got up again."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Vinicius rushed at Lygia. Ursus grabbed him and threw him to the ground. Vinicius's arm broke, and his head struck the floor."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Ursus raised his fist over the man who had tried to take Lygia."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"lygia","e":"shock","t":"Ursus! No! Don't kill him! Christ forbids it!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"And the giant stopped. He lowered his fist. He picked Vinicius up as gently as a child and laid him on a bed."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Ursus was strong enough to crush a gladiator. But he was even stronger at something else: obeying Christ when he was angry."}],"quote":{"text":"Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.","who":"Romans 12:21","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Strength under control","text":"Ursus could have killed Vinicius, and some would say he had every right. But at Lygia's word, 'Christ forbids it', he stopped. The strongest person in the room is the one who can control their anger."},"think":"Ursus was strong enough to win any fight. Why is choosing NOT to hurt someone sometimes the stronger choice?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Vinicius follow Lygia?","o":["To a small house across the river","To the palace","To the arena","To the sea"],"why":"After the night meeting."},{"q":"What was Croton supposed to do?","o":["Grab Lygia and deal with the giant","Pray","Guard the door","Cook dinner"],"why":"Vinicius's plan."},{"q":"What happened between Ursus and Croton?","o":["Ursus defeated the gladiator","Croton won easily","They became friends","They both ran away"],"why":"Ursus was stronger."},{"q":"What did Lygia cry out?","o":["Don't kill him! Christ forbids it!","Hit him harder!","Run!","Call the soldiers!"],"why":"Even for her enemy."},{"q":"What did Ursus do then?","o":["Gently laid Vinicius on a bed","Threw him in the river","Locked him outside","Ran away"],"why":"Strength under control."}]},"qv2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Vinicius woke up in pain, in a small, plain room. He expected to be killed, or at least thrown into the street. Instead, someone was gently bandaging his arm."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"It was Glaucus, the Christian doctor, the very man Chilo had betrayed. He was setting the arm of the man who had come to kidnap one of his sisters in Christ."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"ursus","e":"worried","t":"Forgive me, lord. I didn't mean to hurt you so badly. Christ tells us not to kill."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"vinicius","e":"shock","t":"You... you're asking ME to forgive YOU?"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"For days, the Christians cared for him. They brought him food. They prayed for him. And Lygia sat by his bed and looked after him."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"The apostle Peter himself came to visit, and Vinicius met Paul of Tarsus too. Vinicius watched how these people lived. They had nothing to gain from being kind to him. They could have reported him or left him to die."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"vinicius","e":"worried","t":"I came here as their enemy. And they treat me like a brother. Who are these people?"},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"As the days passed, Lygia realised she was beginning to love him. But he didn't know Christ, and she wanted to love Christ first."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"crispus","e":"stern","t":"Lygia, be careful. Guard your heart. He is not a follower of Christ."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"So, before Vinicius was well, Lygia quietly left the house with Ursus. When Vinicius found her gone, his heart broke. But something in it had already begun to change."}],"quote":{"text":"But I say unto you which hear, Love your enemies, do good to them which hate you.","who":"Luke 6:27","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Love that changes enemies","text":"The Christians didn't win Vinicius by arguing. They won him by loving him when he deserved the opposite. And Lygia showed a different kind of courage: she put Christ before her own feelings, even when it hurt."},"think":"Lygia left because she wanted to love Christ first. Why is it wise to think about faith and values before falling for someone?","quiz":[{"q":"Who bandaged Vinicius's broken arm?","o":["Glaucus, the Christian doctor","Croton","Nero's doctor","Petronius"],"why":"The man Chilo had betrayed."},{"q":"What did Ursus say to Vinicius?","o":["Forgive me","I'll finish you later","Go home","Pay me"],"why":"Christ tells us not to kill."},{"q":"Which apostles did Vinicius meet while he was recovering?","o":["Peter and Paul","John and James","Thomas and Andrew","None"],"why":"They visited the house."},{"q":"What amazed Vinicius about the Christians?","o":["They treated their enemy like a brother","They were rich","They fought well","They ignored him"],"why":"Love he could not explain."},{"q":"Why did Lygia leave before he was well?","o":["She wanted to love Christ first","She was angry","She was scared of Ursus","Nero called her"],"why":"Faith before feelings."}]}}},"qv3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Vinicius stop doing to his slaves?","o":["Having them beaten","Feeding them","Paying them","Talking to them"],"why":"His heart was changing."},{"q":"What did Paul teach Vinicius?","o":["Anyone in Christ becomes new","Only Jews can be saved","Rome is holy","Obey Nero"],"why":"2 Corinthians 5:17."},{"q":"What did Peter say about Vinicius's love for Lygia?","o":["Love her in Christ, and Christ will bless it","Forget her","Marry quickly","Ask Nero"],"why":"Love made new."},{"q":"Where was Vinicius when Rome caught fire?","o":["At Antium with Nero's court","In Lygia's house","In Sicily","In prison"],"why":"He rushed back."},{"q":"What happened to Vinicius's horse?","o":["It collapsed from exhaustion","It ran away","It flew","It was stolen"],"why":"He ran the rest of the way."},{"q":"Where did Vinicius find Lygia?","o":["With Peter and the Christians outside the city","In the palace","In the river","In the arena"],"why":"Safe with Ursus."},{"q":"Who baptised Vinicius?","o":["Peter","Paul","Ursus","Glaucus"],"why":"He belonged to Christ now."},{"q":"What did Nero supposedly sing about while Rome burned?","o":["The burning of Troy","The sea","Peace","His mother"],"why":"That's how people remembered it."},{"q":"Who offered to name the Christians?","o":["Chilo","Acte","Petronius","Glaucus"],"why":"For revenge and gold."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Weeping may endure for a night, but ___ cometh in the morning.\"","o":["joy","rain","fear","night"],"why":"Psalm 30:5."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! In what year did the great fire of Rome happen?","o":["A.D. 64","A.D. 1964","100 B.C.","A.D. 500"],"why":"During Nero's rule."},"choices":[{"title":"How you treat the cleaner","q":"Your school cleaner accidentally knocks your bag over and your books get wet. Your friends expect you to shout at her.","o":[{"t":"Say, \"It's okay, accidents happen,\" and help pick things up.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Vinicius's change showed first in how he treated people with less power."},{"t":"Shout at her so your friends see you're tough.","f":"That's the old Vinicius."},{"t":"Report her to the principal.","f":"For an accident? Grace is better."}]},{"title":"The blame game","q":"A window in your class gets broken. The teacher is angry. Everyone starts pointing at a quiet boy who wasn't even there.","o":[{"t":"Speak up: \"It wasn't him. He wasn't here.\"","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You refused to let an innocent person become the scapegoat."},{"t":"Point at him too, so you don't get blamed.","f":"That's what Rome did to the Christians."},{"t":"Stay quiet. It's not your problem.","f":"Silence helped the lie win."}]},{"title":"In a crisis","q":"There's a fire alarm at school and everyone panics. Some younger pupils are crying and don't know where to go.","o":[{"t":"Stay calm, take their hands, and lead them to the assembly point.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Peter in the smoke, a calm heart helps others."},{"t":"Run ahead and save yourself.","f":"Your own safety matters, but so do the little ones beside you."},{"t":"Film it on your phone.","f":"Not the time!"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of Quo Vadis in real life."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🌱 Real change shows. Let Jesus change how you treat people who can't do anything for you."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"🔥 Love runs towards those in need, not away from them."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"🧘 In a crisis, be calm, pray, and help others through."},{"sc":"palace","n":"🎯 Never let an innocent person be blamed. Speak up for the truth."}],"stops":{"qv3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Vinicius went home. But he was not the same man who had left."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Before, if a slave made a mistake, Vinicius would have him beaten. Now he couldn't do it. He kept hearing Peter's words: love one another."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"romanslave","e":"shock","t":"My master didn't punish me? What has happened to him?"},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"petronius","e":"worried","t":"Nephew, you've changed. You're quieter. Kinder. Are you ill?"},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"vinicius","e":"smile","t":"No, uncle. I think I'm getting well for the first time."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Vinicius went looking for Paul and listened to him for hours. Paul explained that Christ died for proud Romans too, and that anyone can become new."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"paul","e":"smile","t":"If any man is in Christ, he is a new creature. The old things pass away. All things become new."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"At last Vinicius found Lygia again, with Peter. He didn't come to grab her this time. He came humbly, asking for nothing, saying he wanted to follow Christ."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"Love her in Christ, my son, and Christ will bless your love."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Lygia's eyes filled with tears. The man who had treated her as a prize now treated her as a sister in Christ, and he loved her truly."}],"quote":{"text":"Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.","who":"2 Corinthians 5:17","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Real change shows","text":"You could see Vinicius's change in how he treated slaves, how he spoke and how he loved. When Jesus changes a heart, it shows in ordinary things: how we treat people with less power than us."},"think":"Vinicius's change showed first in how he treated his slaves. How do we treat people who can't do anything for us? What does that reveal?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the first sign that Vinicius had changed?","o":["He stopped having his slaves beaten","He bought a new house","He became a senator","He sang for Nero"],"why":"Love one another."},{"q":"What did Petronius think?","o":["That Vinicius might be ill","That he was a hero","That he should be arrested","Nothing"],"why":"He didn't understand the change."},{"q":"Who did Vinicius listen to for hours?","o":["Paul","Chilo","Nero","Croton"],"why":"Paul explained the new life in Christ."},{"q":"How did Vinicius come to Lygia this time?","o":["Humbly, wanting to follow Christ","With soldiers","With gold","With a threat"],"why":"Not to grab, but to love."},{"q":"What does 2 Corinthians 5:17 say about anyone in Christ?","o":["He is a new creature","He stays the same","He becomes rich","He never struggles"],"why":"Old things pass away."}]},"qv3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"palace","n":"Then Nero ordered his whole court to follow him to {Antium}, a town by the sea. Vinicius had to go, leaving Lygia behind in Rome."},{"sc":"palace","n":"One evening a messenger galloped in, covered in dust."},{"sc":"palace","w":"romanslave","e":"shock","t":"Rome is burning! The whole city is on fire!"},{"sc":"road","n":"Vinicius didn't wait for permission. He leapt on a horse and rode through the night. He rode so hard that his horse collapsed, and he ran on foot."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"When he reached Rome, he saw a sea of fire. Whole streets were burning. Crowds were screaming and running with whatever they could carry."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"Smoke filled the air. Buildings crashed down. People fled towards the river and the fields outside the walls."},{"sc":"romefire","w":"vinicius","e":"worried","t":"Lygia's house is across the river. Lord Christ, keep her safe. Show me where she is!"},{"sc":"romefire","n":"Vinicius covered his face with a wet cloth and pushed straight into the burning city, against the crowds, through the heat and the falling sparks."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"This was the man who had once wanted Lygia as a prize. Now he was ready to die to save her."}],"quote":{"text":"When thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.","who":"Isaiah 43:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Love runs towards","text":"When Rome caught fire, everyone ran away from it. Vinicius ran into it, praying, to find the one he loved. Real love is willing to sacrifice. And God promises to be with us even when we walk through fire."},"think":"Compare Vinicius in Chapter 1 with Vinicius here. What made the difference?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Nero's court when the fire started?","o":["At Antium, by the sea","In Rome","In Egypt","In Sicily"],"why":"Vinicius had to go with them."},{"q":"What did Vinicius do when he heard the news?","o":["Rode through the night to Rome","Stayed at Antium","Sent a letter","Went to sleep"],"why":"His horse collapsed and he ran on."},{"q":"What did Vinicius find in Rome?","o":["A sea of fire","A peaceful city","A party","An empty city"],"why":"Whole streets were burning."},{"q":"What did he pray?","o":["Lord Christ, keep her safe","Save my house","Let Nero win","Nothing"],"why":"He prayed for Lygia."},{"q":"What does Isaiah 43:2 promise?","o":["When you walk through fire, you will not be burned","There will be no fire","Run from every danger","Fire is good"],"why":"God is with us in it."}]},"qv3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"romefire","n":"Vinicius fought his way across the river to Lygia's street. Her house was empty. Fire was racing towards it."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"He nearly collapsed from the heat and smoke. Then, out of the chaos, he heard that the Christians had gathered outside the city, where Peter was."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"There he found a huge crowd of homeless, frightened people. And in the middle stood the old apostle, calm as a rock, praying with them and comforting them."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"Do not fear. Christ is with us. This city may burn, but his kingdom cannot."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"And there, beside Peter, safe, with Ursus close by, was Lygia."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"lygia","e":"big","t":"Marcus! You came through the fire for me!"},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"vinicius","e":"big","t":"Thank God. Thank Christ. You're alive."},{"sc":"river","n":"Soon after, Peter baptised Vinicius. The proud Roman soldier went down into the water and came up a follower of Jesus."},{"sc":"river","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"Go in peace, my son. You belong to Christ now."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Rome burned for six days. Thousands lost everything. But in the middle of the smoke, Vinicius found the two things he had been searching for: Lygia, and Christ."}],"quote":{"text":"Weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.","who":"Psalm 30:5","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Calm in the chaos","text":"While Rome panicked, Peter stood calm among frightened people, praying and comforting. Faith doesn't stop disasters from happening. But it gives you a steady heart to help others through them."},"think":"Peter stayed calm when everyone else panicked. When there's a crisis at home or school, how could you be a calm, helpful presence?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Vinicius find at Lygia's house?","o":["It was empty, with fire coming","Lygia asleep","Nero","Chilo"],"why":"She had already gone."},{"q":"Where were the Christians?","o":["Gathered outside the city with Peter","In the palace","On ships","In the arena"],"why":"Peter was comforting them."},{"q":"What did Peter say?","o":["This city may burn, but his kingdom cannot","Run for your lives","It's your fault","Go home"],"why":"Calm in the chaos."},{"q":"What happened to Vinicius soon after?","o":["Peter baptised him","He was arrested","He went back to Nero","He left Rome for ever"],"why":"He belonged to Christ now."},{"q":"How long did Rome burn?","o":["Six days","One hour","Six months","Two years"],"why":"Thousands lost everything."}]},"qv3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"romefire","n":"As Rome burned, Nero came back. People said he stood on a high tower in costume, watching the flames and singing a song about the burning of {Troy}."},{"sc":"romefire","n":"Nobody knows exactly how the fire started. But the homeless crowds began to whisper: 'Nero did it. He wanted to rebuild Rome his way.'"},{"sc":"palace","n":"Nero grew frightened. The people's anger could cost him his throne. He needed someone to blame."},{"sc":"palace","w":"tigellinus","e":"smirk","t":"There's a strange group in the city, Caesar. The Christians. They refuse to worship you. They meet in secret. People already distrust them."},{"sc":"palace","w":"poppaea","e":"smirk","t":"Blame them. Then give the people a show in the arena. They'll forget their anger."},{"sc":"palace","n":"And then Chilo stepped forward. Vinicius had once had him beaten for his lies, and Chilo had never forgiven it. Now he saw his chance for revenge, and for gold."},{"sc":"palace","w":"chilo","e":"smirk","t":"I know where they meet. I know their names. I know their secret signs."},{"sc":"palace","w":"nero","e":"big","t":"Then let it be the Christians. Arrest them all!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"The Christians were innocent. But they became the {scapegoat} for a crime they didn't commit. A terrible persecution was about to begin."}],"quote":{"text":"Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake.","who":"Matthew 5:11","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"When you're falsely blamed","text":"The Christians were blamed for a fire they didn't start, simply because they were different and easy to accuse. Jesus warned this would happen. Stay honest, stay kind, and remember that God sees the truth."},"think":"Why do people in trouble often look for someone else to blame? Who tends to get blamed unfairly in a school or community?","quiz":[{"q":"What were people saying about Nero?","o":["That he started the fire","That he saved the city","That he was kind","That he was asleep"],"why":"He needed someone else to blame."},{"q":"Who suggested blaming the Christians?","o":["Tigellinus and Poppaea","Peter","Petronius","Lygia"],"why":"Cruel advisers."},{"q":"Why did Chilo betray the Christians?","o":["Revenge and gold","He was forced","To protect them","By accident"],"why":"He had never forgiven his beating."},{"q":"What is a scapegoat?","o":["Someone blamed for what others did","A kind of animal at the market","A hero","A soldier"],"why":"The Christians were innocent."},{"q":"What does Jesus say about people falsely accused for his sake?","o":["They are blessed","They are cursed","They are forgotten","They should fight back"],"why":"Matthew 5:11."}]}}},"qv4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who led the soldiers to the Christians?","o":["Chilo","Petronius","Acte","Glaucus"],"why":"He knew all their signs."},{"q":"Which prison was Lygia thrown into?","o":["The Tullianum","The Bastille","The Tower of London","None"],"why":"A dark prison under Rome."},{"q":"Why couldn't Petronius save Lygia?","o":["Poppaea hated her","He didn't care","He was a Christian","He was ill"],"why":"Nero listened to Poppaea."},{"q":"What did the Christians do in prison?","o":["Prayed and sang hymns","Plotted revenge","Fought the guards","Gave up"],"why":"The guards had never seen prisoners like them."},{"q":"What did the Christians cry out in the arena?","o":["Christus regnat! (Christ reigns!)","Save us, Nero!","Run!","We're sorry!"],"why":"Faith instead of fear."},{"q":"What are martyrs?","o":["People killed because they will not give up their faith","Soldiers","Singers","Rulers"],"why":"Many early Christians were martyrs."},{"q":"What did Glaucus say to Chilo?","o":["I forgive","Go away","You'll pay","Nothing"],"why":"Two powerful words."},{"q":"Who baptised Chilo?","o":["Paul","Peter","Nero","Vinicius"],"why":"Christ forgives even him."},{"q":"What animal did Ursus fight?","o":["A wild aurochs bull","A lion","A bear","A crocodile"],"why":"With his bare hands."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"We are more than ___ through him that loved us.\"","o":["conquerors","soldiers","winners","friends"],"why":"Romans 8:37."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Why did Nero finally let Lygia, Ursus and Vinicius live?","o":["The huge crowd demanded mercy","Poppaea asked him","Peter told him to","He felt sorry"],"why":"Even an emperor feared that crowd."},"choices":[{"title":"Mocked for your faith online","q":"Someone posts a meme mocking Christians and tags you. People are laughing in the comments.","o":[{"t":"Don't hit back with insults. If you reply, be calm and kind, or let it go and pray for them.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The Christians in the arena answered cruelty with courage and kindness."},{"t":"Post an even nastier meme about them.","f":"That's answering evil with evil."},{"t":"Delete your church photos so nobody knows.","f":"Hiding out of fear isn't the way of the martyrs."}]},{"title":"The worst person you know","q":"A classmate who has lied about you and stolen from you comes to you crying because his parents are divorcing.","o":[{"t":"Listen to him, be kind, and tell him God loves him.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Glaucus's two words broke Chilo's heart open. Your kindness might do the same."},{"t":"Tell him it serves him right.","f":"Chilo deserved far worse, and Glaucus forgave."},{"t":"Pretend you didn't hear him.","f":"This might be his 'Chilo's night'."}]},{"title":"Preparing for pressure","q":"You know that at a sleepover this weekend, people will pressure you to watch something you shouldn't.","o":[{"t":"Pray beforehand, decide your 'no' now, and plan what you'll say or do.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Ursus knelt and prayed before the bull came out."},{"t":"Hope it doesn't happen.","f":"Hope isn't a plan."},{"t":"Decide you'll just go along with it.","f":"That's giving up before the battle."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"dungeon","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 4 of Quo Vadis in real life."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"⛓️ In your darkest valley, you are not alone. He is with you."},{"sc":"arena","n":"🎶 Answer cruelty with courage and kindness, not with more cruelty."},{"sc":"torches","n":"🕊️ Forgive. Two words can change a heart: 'I forgive.'"},{"sc":"arena","n":"🐂 Pray before your battles. God gives strength to those who trust him."}],"stops":{"qv4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"townnight","n":"Chilo led the soldiers from house to house. He knew the fish signs, the meeting places, the names."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"Thousands of Christians were arrested: men, women, children, slaves and free. Their only crime was following Jesus."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"Soldiers burst into the house where Lygia was staying. Ursus could have fought them all. But Lygia told him not to, and they were both taken away."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"They were thrown into the {Tullianum}, a dark, crowded prison under the city. Then Lygia fell sick with a terrible fever."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"vinicius","e":"worried","t":"Uncle, please! You're Nero's friend. Beg him to free her!"},{"sc":"palace","w":"petronius","e":"worried","t":"I tried, Marcus. But Poppaea hates her, and Nero listens to Poppaea. I'm afraid I have made things worse."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"Vinicius tried everything: bribes, plans, secret tunnels. Nothing worked. At last he went to the prison and, with gold, got in to see her."},{"sc":"dungeon","w":"lygia","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid for me, Marcus. Whether I live or die, I belong to Christ. And so do you."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"In that dark prison, the Christians prayed and sang hymns together. The guards had never seen prisoners like them."}],"quote":{"text":"Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me.","who":"Psalm 23:4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Not alone in the dark","text":"Lygia lost her freedom and her health in a dark prison. Yet she comforted Vinicius instead of the other way round. Faith doesn't make the valley disappear. It means we never walk through it alone."},"think":"Lygia comforted Vinicius even though she was the one in prison. Where do you think that kind of peace comes from?","quiz":[{"q":"How did the soldiers find the Christians?","o":["Chilo led them","They used dogs","Lygia told them","By chance"],"why":"He knew their signs and names."},{"q":"Why didn't Ursus fight the soldiers?","o":["Lygia told him not to","He was asleep","He was afraid","He wasn't there"],"why":"He obeyed her, and Christ."},{"q":"What happened to Lygia in prison?","o":["She fell sick with a fever","She escaped","She was freed","She became a guard"],"why":"A dark, crowded prison."},{"q":"Why couldn't Petronius free her?","o":["Poppaea hated her, and Nero listened to Poppaea","He didn't try","He was in Egypt","He agreed with Nero"],"why":"He tried and failed."},{"q":"What did Lygia tell Vinicius?","o":["Whether I live or die, I belong to Christ","Get me out!","It's your fault","Forget me"],"why":"Peace in the dark."}]},"qv4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"arena","n":"Then the games began. The amphitheatre filled with tens of thousands of people. Nero sat in his purple box, looking down."},{"sc":"arena","n":"The crowd had come to see the Christians suffer for the fire. Nero's {persecution} was meant to be a show."},{"sc":"arena","n":"We won't describe the cruel things that were done that day. Many Christians died. They are remembered as {martyrs}."},{"sc":"arena","n":"But something happened that the crowd did not expect. The Christians did not beg. They did not curse. They knelt down together and sang."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Some of them cried out to the crowd: '{Christus regnat}!' Christ reigns!"},{"sc":"arena","n":"Some people in the crowd laughed. But others fell silent. A few began to ask in their hearts: 'What kind of faith makes people sing as they die?'"},{"sc":"arena","w":"vinicius","e":"worried","t":"Lord, give them strength. And give me strength to watch, and to keep believing."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Lygia was not called out that day. Her fever was so bad that the guards thought she would die in prison anyway. In a strange way, the sickness saved her life, for now."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Nero's plan was to make people hate the Christians. But their courage made many people wonder about Jesus. Their faith became a witness."}],"quote":{"text":"Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him that loved us.","who":"Romans 8:37","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Faith that sings","text":"Nero wanted a show of fear. He got a show of faith instead. The early Christians changed the Roman world not by fighting, but by loving, forgiving and staying faithful to death. Their courage still speaks today."},"think":"Why do you think the courage of the Christians made some people in the crowd start asking questions about Jesus?","proverb":{"text":"Igwe bụ ike.","lang":"Igbo","mean":"Unity is strength. Together we are strong."},"quiz":[{"q":"Why had the crowd come to the arena?","o":["To see the Christians suffer for the fire","To hear music","To see a race","To vote"],"why":"Nero's cruel show."},{"q":"What did the Christians do?","o":["Knelt together and sang","Begged for mercy","Cursed Nero","Fought the guards"],"why":"Faith instead of fear."},{"q":"What does 'Christus regnat' mean?","o":["Christ reigns","Caesar rules","Help us","Goodbye"],"why":"Their cry of faith."},{"q":"Why wasn't Lygia taken out that day?","o":["Her fever was so bad the guards thought she would die anyway","She escaped","Vinicius bribed Nero","She hid"],"why":"The sickness saved her, for now."},{"q":"What does the Igbo proverb 'Igwe bụ ike' mean?","o":["Unity is strength","Iron is heavy","Run fast","Sing loudly"],"why":"The Christians stood together."}]},"qv4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"torches","n":"One night, Nero held a party in his gardens. The gardens were lit by torches, and some of those burning torches were Christians, tied to posts. It was one of the cruellest things Nero ever did."},{"sc":"torches","n":"Chilo walked beside Nero, honoured as the man who had found the Christians. But Chilo's face was pale. His heart was pounding."},{"sc":"torches","n":"At one of the posts, Chilo saw a face he knew. It was Glaucus, the doctor he had betrayed long ago, and betrayed again."},{"sc":"torches","n":"Glaucus looked down at Chilo. He didn't curse him. He spoke two words:"},{"sc":"torches","w":"glaucus","e":"smile","t":"I forgive."},{"sc":"torches","n":"Something broke inside Chilo. He turned to the crowd and screamed with all his strength:"},{"sc":"torches","w":"chilo","e":"shock","t":"People of Rome! The Christians are innocent! It was Nero who burned the city!"},{"sc":"night","n":"Then Chilo ran off into the dark, terrified, and fell down weeping. A man found him there. It was the apostle Paul."},{"sc":"night","w":"paul","e":"smile","t":"Chilo, Christ forgives even you. There is no sin so great that his mercy cannot reach it."},{"sc":"night","w":"chilo","e":"worried","t":"Even me? After everything I've done?"},{"sc":"night","n":"Paul baptised him that night. Soon after, Chilo was arrested. They demanded that he take back his words about Nero. He refused. He died as a follower of Jesus, as bravely as the people he had once betrayed."}],"quote":{"text":"Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do.","who":"Luke 23:34","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Forgiveness is powerful","text":"Chilo was a liar, a cheat and a betrayer. Two words from a man he had wronged, 'I forgive', did what no punishment could: they broke his heart open. Forgiveness is not weakness. It's one of the most powerful things in the world."},"think":"Is anyone too bad to be forgiven by God? What does Chilo's story tell you?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Chilo see Glaucus?","o":["In Nero's gardens, tied to a burning post","At the market","In church","On a ship"],"why":"One of Nero's cruellest acts."},{"q":"What did Glaucus say to Chilo?","o":["I forgive","I curse you","Help me","Run"],"why":"Two words that broke Chilo's heart."},{"q":"What did Chilo shout to the crowd?","o":["The Christians are innocent! Nero burned the city!","Long live Nero!","Kill them all!","I'm rich!"],"why":"The truth at last."},{"q":"Who found Chilo weeping in the dark?","o":["Paul","Nero","Vinicius","Croton"],"why":"And told him Christ forgives even him."},{"q":"How did Chilo die?","o":["As a follower of Jesus, refusing to take back the truth","As a rich man","Running away","Laughing"],"why":"As brave as those he had betrayed."}]},"qv4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"arena","n":"Lygia's fever passed. And Poppaea made sure she was saved for the biggest show of all."},{"sc":"arena","n":"On the last day of the games, the crowd roared as Ursus walked out alone onto the sand. The giant had no weapon. He knelt and prayed."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Then a gate opened. A huge wild {aurochs} bull charged out. And tied to its great horns was Lygia."},{"sc":"arena","w":"vinicius","e":"shock","t":"Lygia! Lord Christ, save her!"},{"sc":"arena","n":"Ursus leapt up. He ran straight at the charging bull and grabbed it by the horns."},{"sc":"arena","n":"The crowd fell silent. The giant and the beast strained against each other. Ursus's feet sank into the sand. His muscles shook. Slowly, slowly, he twisted the bull's head."},{"sc":"arena","n":"With a terrible crack, the bull fell. Ursus untied Lygia, lifted her gently in his arms, and held her up towards the crowd, as if asking for mercy."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Then Vinicius leapt down onto the sand, tore open his tunic to show his scars from fighting for Rome, and stood beside them."},{"sc":"arena","n":"The crowd went wild. Thousands of people shouted: 'Mercy! Mercy! Give them their lives!'"},{"sc":"arena","w":"nero","e":"frown","t":"Very well. Let them live."},{"sc":"arena","n":"Nero didn't want to. But even an emperor was afraid of that crowd. Lygia, Ursus and Vinicius walked out of the arena alive."}],"quote":{"text":"Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee.","who":"Isaiah 41:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God's strength","text":"Ursus faced the bull with no weapon but his faith and the strength God gave him. Not every martyr was rescued. But on that day, God used one faithful giant to save Lygia, and an entire crowd changed its mind."},"think":"Ursus knelt and prayed before the bull came out. What 'bulls' do you face, and how could you prepare for them?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Ursus do before the bull came out?","o":["Knelt and prayed","Ran away","Picked up a sword","Waved at Nero"],"why":"He prepared with prayer."},{"q":"What was tied to the bull's horns?","o":["Lygia","A flag","A rope","A crown"],"why":"Poppaea's cruel plan."},{"q":"How did Ursus stop the bull?","o":["He twisted its head until it fell","With a spear","He tamed it with food","He jumped over it"],"why":"God gave him strength."},{"q":"What did the crowd shout?","o":["Mercy!","Kill them!","Long live Poppaea!","Again!"],"why":"Even the crowd was moved."},{"q":"What does Isaiah 41:10 promise?","o":["I will strengthen thee and help thee","You'll never face danger","Run away","Be strong by yourself"],"why":"Fear not, for I am with thee."}]}}},"qv5":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where did Vinicius and Lygia live after the arena?","o":["Sicily","Rome","Antium","Britain"],"why":"Far from Nero."},{"q":"How did Petronius feel about the Christians?","o":["He respected them but never followed Christ","He hated them","He became their leader","He never heard of them"],"why":"Admiring is not following."},{"q":"Why did the Christians urge Peter to leave Rome?","o":["To save his life","He was lazy","He had a cold","Nero invited him away"],"why":"They loved their shepherd."},{"q":"What time of day did Peter meet Jesus on the road?","o":["Sunrise","Midnight","Noon","Evening"],"why":"In the golden light."},{"q":"Who walked with Peter?","o":["Nazarius","Chilo","Ursus","Glaucus"],"why":"A boy who didn't see what Peter saw."},{"q":"What did Jesus say he was going to Rome to do?","o":["Be crucified a second time","Rule as king","Burn the city","Rescue Nero"],"why":"If Peter deserted his people."},{"q":"Where did Peter go after the vision?","o":["Back to Rome","To Sicily","To Jerusalem","To Antium"],"why":"Quo vadis? To Rome."},{"q":"How did Peter die?","o":["Crucified upside down","Of old age","In a fire","In the arena with Ursus"],"why":"He felt unworthy to die like Jesus."},{"q":"How does Sienkiewicz describe Nero's passing?","o":["Like a whirlwind, a storm, a fire or a war","Like a gentle breeze","Like a king's crowning","He doesn't mention it"],"why":"And then he was gone."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"The good shepherd giveth his ___ for the sheep.\"","o":["life","food","time","staff"],"why":"John 10:11."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What Latin cry of the martyrs means 'Christ reigns'?","o":["Christus regnat","Quo vadis","Ave Caesar","Carpe diem"],"why":"And he still does."},"choices":[{"title":"Running away","q":"You're the leader of your school's Christian fellowship. It's been hard: few people come, some mock you, and you want to quit.","o":[{"t":"Pray, tell a mentor how you feel, and stay with the people God has given you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Peter, you turned back towards the people Jesus loves."},{"t":"Quit quietly and let someone else handle it.","f":"Sometimes stepping down is right, but ask Jesus first: 'Quo vadis?'"},{"t":"Blame the members for not caring.","f":"A shepherd cares for the sheep, even weak ones."}]},{"title":"Admiring vs following","q":"Your friend says, \"I think Jesus was a great teacher, like a role model. But I don't need to follow him or go to church.\"","o":[{"t":"Kindly share Petronius's story: admiring Jesus isn't the same as following him.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You gently invited your friend from admiring to following."},{"t":"Agree. Admiring is enough.","f":"Petronius thought so too, and missed the life Vinicius found."},{"t":"Tell them they're going to hell.","f":"Truth spoken without love rarely opens a heart."}]},{"title":"Impressed by power","q":"A rich, famous influencer brags about cheating people and being cruel, and lots of students copy his style and attitude.","o":[{"t":"Don't copy him. Choose to follow Jesus' way of humble, loving strength.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Nero had power. Peter had faith. Guess who's remembered with love."},{"t":"Copy him. Power is power.","f":"Nero thought that too."},{"t":"Follow him online just for fun.","f":"What you feed on shapes you."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"seashore","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's how you'll use Quo Vadis for the rest of your life."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"🚶 Don't just admire Jesus. Follow him."},{"sc":"appian","n":"❓ Ask yourself often: 'Quo vadis? Where am I going?' Then walk where Jesus is going."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"🐑 Stay with the people God has given you to care for, even when it's hard."},{"sc":"rome","n":"🪨 Empires fall, but Christ's church stands. Christus regnat!"},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"👑 Well done! You've finished Quo Vadis."}],"stops":{"qv5s1":{"story":[{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"Lygia was weak but alive. Vinicius carried her home himself, with Ursus walking beside them like a mountain."},{"sc":"romanvilla","w":"lygia","e":"smile","t":"Marcus, God gave us our lives back. Let's use them for him."},{"sc":"romanvilla","n":"But Rome was still dangerous. As soon as Lygia could travel, they slipped away to {Sicily}, far from Nero, where Vinicius had a house among the hills by the sea."},{"sc":"seashore","n":"There they married, and they lived quietly and happily, caring for others and following Christ. Ursus lived with them, as gentle as ever."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Petronius was not so blessed. He had never become a Christian. He lost Nero's favour, and soon after, he died."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"In his letters to Vinicius, Petronius admitted that he could not understand the Christians or their courage. He respected them. But he never came to Christ himself."},{"sc":"seashore","n":"Two men from the same family. Both heard about Jesus. One followed him and found life. The other admired from a distance and missed it."}],"quote":{"text":"The LORD hath done great things for us; whereof we are glad.","who":"Psalm 126:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Admiring isn't following","text":"Petronius admired the Christians' courage but never gave his life to Christ. Vinicius did, and everything changed. It's not enough to admire Jesus from a distance. He invites you to follow him."},"think":"Petronius thought the Christians were impressive, but he never followed Jesus. Why do you think some people admire Jesus but don't follow him?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Vinicius and Lygia go to be safe?","o":["Sicily","Egypt","Antium","Britain"],"why":"Far from Nero."},{"q":"Who lived with them?","o":["Ursus","Chilo","Nero","Poppaea"],"why":"As gentle as ever."},{"q":"What did Lygia say God had given them?","o":["Their lives back","Gold","A palace","Fame"],"why":"To use for him."},{"q":"What happened to Petronius?","o":["He lost Nero's favour and died, never becoming a Christian","He became a bishop","He became emperor","He moved to Sicily"],"why":"He admired but never followed."},{"q":"What is the lesson of Petronius and Vinicius?","o":["Admiring Jesus isn't the same as following him","Uncles are always wrong","Rome is bad","Never write letters"],"why":"Follow, don't just admire."}]},"qv5s2":{"story":[{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Back in Rome, the persecution went on. The Christians who were left were afraid for Peter, their old shepherd."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"crispus","e":"worried","t":"Peter, Nero is hunting for you. If they catch you, you will die. Please, leave Rome. The church everywhere needs you."},{"sc":"ostrianum","n":"Peter was very old and very tired. He had seen so many of his friends die. At last, he agreed."},{"sc":"ostrianum","w":"peter","e":"worried","t":"If you think it best, I will go."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Before sunrise, Peter slipped out of the city with a boy named Nazarius. They walked along the {Appian Way}, the great road south."},{"sc":"appian","w":"nazarius","e":"smile","t":"We're nearly out, teacher. Soon you'll be safe."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Peter walked slowly, leaning on his staff. Behind him lay Rome, the city where his people were suffering. Ahead lay safety."},{"sc":"appian","n":"It wasn't wrong for the Christians to want to save him. They loved him. But Peter was about to find out what Jesus wanted."}],"quote":{"text":"Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.","who":"Matthew 26:41","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Even the strong get tired","text":"Peter, the great apostle, was old, tired and heartbroken. He agreed to run. Even the strongest believers have moments of weakness. God doesn't throw them away. He meets them on the road."},"think":"Why do you think Peter agreed to leave? Have you ever been so tired of a hard situation that you just wanted to escape it?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did the Christians want Peter to leave Rome?","o":["Nero was hunting him and they loved him","They were tired of him","He was rude","He wanted a holiday"],"why":"They wanted to save their shepherd."},{"q":"How did Peter feel?","o":["Very old, tired and heartbroken","Excited","Angry","Bored"],"why":"He had seen so many friends die."},{"q":"Who walked with Peter?","o":["A boy named Nazarius","Ursus","Vinicius","Paul"],"why":"Before sunrise."},{"q":"Which road did they take?","o":["The Appian Way","The Silk Road","The Ear-gate road","The river"],"why":"The great road south."},{"q":"What does Matthew 26:41 say about the flesh?","o":["The flesh is weak","The flesh is strong","The flesh is evil","The flesh is perfect"],"why":"But the spirit is willing."}]},"qv5s3":{"story":[{"sc":"appian","n":"As the sun began to rise, Peter suddenly stopped. He stared down the road, his face shining."},{"sc":"appian","w":"nazarius","e":"worried","t":"Teacher? What is it? I don't see anything."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Coming towards them along the road, in the golden light, Peter saw Jesus, walking towards Rome."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Peter fell to his knees. And he asked the question that gives this book its name:"},{"sc":"appian","w":"peter","e":"shock","t":"{Quo vadis, Domine?} Where are you going, Lord?"},{"sc":"appian","w":"jesusqv","e":"smile","t":"If you desert my people, I am going to Rome to be crucified a second time."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Peter lay with his face in the dust for a long time. Nazarius didn't understand what had happened."},{"sc":"appian","n":"When Peter stood up, his tiredness had gone. He picked up his staff and turned around, back towards the city."},{"sc":"appian","w":"nazarius","e":"shock","t":"Quo vadis, domine? Where are you going, teacher?"},{"sc":"appian","w":"peter","e":"smile","t":"To Rome."},{"sc":"appian","n":"Years before, Peter had run away from Jesus' cross. Now he walked back towards his own, to stay with the people Jesus had given him to care for."}],"quote":{"text":"Quo vadis, Domine?","who":"Peter","tag":"Sienkiewicz's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Where are you going?","text":"Jesus didn't scold Peter. He just showed him where he himself was going: towards his suffering people. 'Quo vadis?' is a question for all of us. Am I running away from where God has placed me, or walking with Jesus towards the people he loves?"},"think":"If Jesus asked you today, 'Where are you going?', what would your honest answer be?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did Peter see on the road?","o":["Jesus, walking towards Rome","Nero","A soldier","Vinicius"],"why":"In the golden light of dawn."},{"q":"What does 'Quo vadis, Domine?' mean?","o":["Where are you going, Lord?","Who are you, Lord?","Help me, Lord!","Goodbye, Lord"],"why":"The book takes its name from it."},{"q":"What did Jesus answer?","o":["If you desert my people, I am going to Rome to be crucified again","Run faster","Go home and rest","Rome is lost"],"why":"He was going to his suffering people."},{"q":"What did Peter do then?","o":["Turned around and went back to Rome","Kept running","Hid in a cave","Went to Sicily"],"why":"To stay with his people."},{"q":"What does the good shepherd do, according to John 10:11?","o":["Gives his life for the sheep","Leaves the sheep","Sells the sheep","Sleeps"],"why":"Jesus did, and Peter followed him."}]},"qv5s4":{"story":[{"sc":"rome","n":"Peter went back into Rome and carried on caring for the Christians. Soon he was arrested."},{"sc":"rome","n":"He was sentenced to be crucified, like his Lord. Peter asked to be crucified upside down. He said he wasn't worthy to die in the same way as Jesus."},{"sc":"rome","n":"On the same day, Paul, as a Roman citizen, was taken outside the city and beheaded. The two great apostles gave their lives in Rome."},{"sc":"palace","n":"And Nero? Four years later, his own people turned against him. The Senate declared him an enemy, and he died alone, hunted and hated."},{"sc":"ruinsfire","n":"Sienkiewicz ends his book by saying that Nero passed away like a whirlwind, a storm, a fire or a war. His palaces fell. His statues were broken. His name became a byword for cruelty."},{"sc":"rome","n":"But on the {Vatican Hill}, where tradition says Peter was buried, a great church now stands. And the faith of the fisherman from Galilee has spread to every nation on earth, including yours."},{"sc":"rome","n":"Jesus once told Peter: 'Upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.'"},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"Empires rise and fall. Emperors come and go. But Christ reigns. 'Christus regnat!' And the people who follow him, like Lygia, Ursus, Vinicius, Chilo and Peter, are never forgotten by him."}],"quote":{"text":"Upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.","who":"Matthew 16:18","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Christ reigns","text":"Nero had all the power in the world, and he is remembered as a monster. Peter had nothing but his faith, and the church he led now fills the world. Don't be impressed by power that hurts people. Stand with Christ. His kingdom lasts for ever."},"think":"Who seemed more powerful in A.D. 64, Nero or Peter? Who seems more powerful now? What does that teach us about true power?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Peter ask to be crucified?","o":["Upside down, because he wasn't worthy to die like Jesus","With a crown","Facing Rome","He wasn't crucified"],"why":"Humble to the end."},{"q":"What happened to Paul?","o":["He was beheaded outside Rome","He escaped to Spain","He became emperor","He went home"],"why":"As a Roman citizen."},{"q":"What happened to Nero four years later?","o":["His people turned against him and he died hunted and hated","He ruled for ever","He became a Christian","He moved to Sicily"],"why":"He passed like a whirlwind."},{"q":"What stands on the Vatican Hill today?","o":["A great church","Nero's palace","An arena","Nothing"],"why":"Where tradition says Peter was buried."},{"q":"What did Jesus say would not prevail against his church?","o":["The gates of hell","The rain","The Romans' law","Time"],"why":"Matthew 16:18."}]}}}});
